  "result": "I added `clamp(cents, low, high)` to the end of `shop/money.py`, and the full test suite passes: 13 tests, all OK, using `python3 -m unittest discover`.\n\n```python\ndef clamp(cents: int, low: int, high: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Limit cents to the inclusive range low..high.\"\"\"\n    if low > high:\n        raise ValueError(f\"low {low} is greater than high {high}\")\n    if cents < low:\n        return low\n    if cents > high:\n        return high\n    return cents\n```\n\nThere was no existing test file for `money.py`, so I created `tests/test_money.py`. It uses `unittest` like the other test files and has 7 tests covering:\n- a value below the range, above it and inside it\n- a value exactly equal to `low` and to `high`\n- `low == high`\n- `low > high`, which raises `ValueError`\n\nNothing is committed.",
